1
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:53,760
Wang Yang.

2
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,760
Wang Yang.

3
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,480
Wang Yang.

4
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,880
Uncle.

5
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:23,880
I'm here for Wang Yang.

6
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,040
Wang Yang's not home.

7
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,120
Then... then I'll get going, uncle.

8
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,080
Hold on.

9
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,320
Where's Wang Yang been going these days? You know?

10
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,600
No idea. I haven't seen him in ages.

11
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,840
Don't feed me a pack of lies.

12
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:40,240
You two are together all day, and you don't know where he goes?

13
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,440
No, uncle, I really don't know.

14
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,240
I haven't seen him in days.

15
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:45,120
Your dad's Qu Zhifei, right?

16
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,400
Works in dispatch.

17
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,240
Every time your dad sees me,

18
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:54,120
it's "Wang-ge" this, "Master Wang" that, always first to say hello.

19
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,200
Did you know that?

20
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:00,080
Should I have your dad join the search?

21
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,080
No, don't. I...

22
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,280
Where are the two of them?

23
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,400
Hey, I'm asking you a damn question.

24
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,600
Where's Shen Mo?

25
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,240
Did something happen to Shen Mo?

26
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,000
I don't know.

27
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:55,640
Jun-ge told me to give you this.

28
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,040
Slow down, uncle.

29
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,400
Turn left up ahead.

30
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:16,880
We're here. This is it.

31
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:25,840
Uncle, I'm not going in.

32
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,240
I've hardly ever been here.

33
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,400
Keep up.

34
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:50,880
Who are you looking for?

35
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,760
I'm looking for Wang Yang.

36
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,400
Dad.

37
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,840
What are you doing here?

38
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:07,760
Come home.

39
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,160
You go on back, Dad.

40
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,680
I'll be home in a bit.

41
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:13,040
Come home.

42
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,480
Dad, I...

43
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,680
Come home.

44
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,760
I...

45
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,600
Don't recognize me anymore?

46
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,040
The police station.

47
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,760
You tried to run,

48
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:29,880
and one trip from me laid you out flat.

49
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,040
Now listen to me.

50
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,600
You're not to see him again.

51
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,320
He's not like you people.

52
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:36,920
Come home.

53
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,360
-But Dad, I've still got things to do.
-Come...

54
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,560
-Come home.
-I...

55
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:41,320
-I said come home.
-I'm really not leaving.

56
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,400
Qu Bo, give me a hand.

57
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,920
Wang Yang, whatever it is, say it at home.

58
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,720
-Wang Yang, talk at home.
-Get lost.

59
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:46,720
Talk at home.

60
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,480
-Who the hell asked you...
-What... what are you doing?

61
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,680
-Asked you to blab to my dad?
-Stop it.

62
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,200
-You just... you fucking...
-What...

63
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:53,520
-What are you doing?
-You and your damn big mouth.

64
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,800
So you've learned to hit people now?

65
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,440
Who taught you that?

66
00:05:58,520 --> 00:05:59,600
Him?

67
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,960
Come home.

68
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,080
Get up now, come on.

69
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,560
You could've really hurt him.

70
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,720
Don't sink to his level.

71
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,240
Come home.

72
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:16,800
Come home.

73
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,680
I'll come home with you.

74
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:25,560
And you, listen to me.

75
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,520
Stay away from him from now on.

76
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,600
You saw it all yourself.

77
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,880
The police bureau, the crime squad —

78
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:32,360
I know them all.

79
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,600
Don't go asking for trouble.

80
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,840
Yang'er.

81
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,600
What happened to you?

82
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,720
Whatever's wrong, you can tell your mom.

83
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,080
I'm fine, Mom.

84
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:53,200
Go to bed.

85
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,240
I'm going to sleep too.

86
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:55,200
Yang'er.

87
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,200
Stop right there.

88
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:00,320
What exactly is going on between you and that man from the video hall?

89
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,920
Nothing's going on.

90
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,520
I'm going to sleep.

91
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,440
Yang'er.

92
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:06,920
Wait, Yang'er.

93
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Yang'er, don't rush off to bed.

94
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,440
Quit wailing my name. Stop pushing me, all right?

95
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:13,000
Is that how you talk to your mom?

96
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,960
Talk to her like that again and I'll break your damn legs.

97
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:18,400
What is going on with you two?

98
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:23,800
You... you go back to the room first.

99
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:24,920
I'll tell you if anything comes up.

100
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,760
Don't lose your temper with him. Talk to him gently.

101
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,200
Go on.

102
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,640
You know how your mom's health is.

103
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,400
Don't make her worry.

104
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:46,280
Let's talk this out, father to son.

105
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:49,680
These past few days —

106
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,600
what have you been up to?

107
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,080
Nothing.

108
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:12,680
Then what's this?

109
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:19,120
What kind of mountain climbing draws blood?

110
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:24,440
Son, did you kill someone?

111
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,480
Son.

112
00:08:42,799 --> 00:08:44,240
I'm your father.

113
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:49,240
Whatever happens to me, I won't let anything happen to you.

114
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:53,960
But you have to tell me the truth first.

115
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,440
You can't keep things from me.

116
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:57,240
Whatever it is, we'll deal with it together.

117
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,480
This is the last chance for you and me.

118
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:04,040
Turning yourself in is nothing like the police coming to arrest you.

119
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,920
Don't do anything stupid, son.

120
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:09,640
Dad.

121
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,520
Just give me two more days.

122
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,760
What do you need two days for?

123
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:20,400
There's still something

124
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,360
I absolutely have to go do.

125
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,320
Until you explain yourself, you're not going anywhere.

126
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:27,800
Dad.

127
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:29,880
I have to go.

128
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:37,320
What... what did you stuff into your pocket back at the video hall?

129
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,320
Take it out...

130
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,080
Who wrote this?

131
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,320
Where are you going on the 17th?

132
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:56,880
Dad.

133
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,680
One day I'll explain everything, I promise.

134
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,880
But right now I really can't say.

135
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,520
Meisu...

136
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,720
-Dad.
-The rope.

137
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,640
-Mom.
-Put this away.

138
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,840
Mom, don't...

139
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,640
Son, just... just bear with it.

140
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,240
-It's all for your own good.
-Dad.

141
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,680
Don't struggle, son.

142
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:28,320
-Don't struggle. Hold still.
-Dad. Mom.

143
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,160
It's for your own good, child.

144
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,440
Whatever you do, don't...

145
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,600
Those rotten things.

146
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:46,440
If he says he didn't kill anyone,

147
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,640
then he didn't.

148
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,880
Our son wouldn't dare kill so much as a chicken.

149
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,640
The two of us believe him.

150
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,600
But will the police?

151
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,400
Will Ma Desheng?

152
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:03,320
Listen to me.

153
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,040
Hasn't he been mixing with bad friends?

154
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,720
He must have been tricked.

155
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,560
It must be that bunch who did it.

156
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,560
Go find Ma Desheng.

157
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:13,800
Tell him

158
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:15,120
to hurry up and arrest those people.

159
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,360
Then our son will be safe.

160
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,880
Tell him our son had nothing to do with it.

161
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,320
-He must have been tricked.
-All right...

162
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,120
-Tell him that and we'll be fine.
-Enough.

163
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,200
Enough...

164
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,000
What do we do?

165
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,480
As for us —

166
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:37,480
we keep the boy locked up for now.

167
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,400
Right under our noses —

168
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,200
that's safest.

169
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:44,680
Then

170
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,200
I'll get to the bottom of this,

171
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,400
and our son will be in the clear.

172
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:59,280
(Take the Hualin freight line on the night of the 17th)

173
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,200
Listen. You hear all that?

174
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:23,560
Hear what?

175
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,360
That's the sound of money,

176
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:31,960
gushing straight into your pocket, Mr. Lu.

177
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:35,400
You're quite the joker, Director Song.

178
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,720
I've signed off on that bank draft, you know.

179
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,680
It'll hit your account right on the 17th.

180
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,440
Wenzhong here keeps his accounts straight.

181
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:46,240
Without you, where would I be?

182
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,160
However deep my pockets get,

183
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:51,440
they're still just your checking account, aren't they, Director Song?

184
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:54,640
Watch your wording.

185
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,880
Building up Hualin Steel is a duty we both share.

186
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,520
Tonight, at the Victoria.

187
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:03,120
Let's have a few extra rounds.

188
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,920
So you're saying it was a misunderstanding?

189
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,440
Yes, a misunderstanding.

190
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,920
Where was your son Wang Yang caught?

191
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,200
The finance office, wasn't it?

192
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:49,000
Yes.

193
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,880
And what does Xing Jianchun do?

194
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,440
Isn't he chief of the security section?

195
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,240
So when he catches your son,

196
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,360
how exactly is that a misunderstanding?

197
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,800
No, Director, here's the thing.

198
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:06,040
Xing Jianchun lured my son to the finance office.

199
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:08,280
He's abusing his post to settle a private score.

200
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,840
You have a private feud with Xing Jianchun?

201
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:13,480
Well, not a feud exactly.

202
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,240
He was reselling factory property,

203
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,360
and I caught him.

204
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:18,080
Viewed from a certain height,

205
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:19,720
I was ridding the people of a menace.

206
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,440
Master Wang.

207
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,360
If Xing Jianchun really has that problem,

208
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,080
I'll chase it down whether you report it or not.

209
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,600
But that's not what we're discussing.

210
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:31,840
We're discussing your son, Wang Yang.

211
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:36,120
Security's finding is that he intended to rob the finance office.

212
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,600
And what is Hualin Steel?

213
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:40,160
Hualin Steel is the face of Hualin.

214
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,560
There's no room in it for people who flirt with crime.

215
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,520
That's the whole of it.

216
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,520
I've made myself clear.

217
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:46,960
I have a meeting. You can go.

218
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,000
Director.

219
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,520
Director.

220
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:05,400
There's one more thing I'd like to clear up.

221
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,640
Go ahead.

222
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:10,040
About that night —

223
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:14,000
I really didn't see anything.

224
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,440
What are you trying to say?

225
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,000
The day I delivered the liquor,

226
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:29,760
I... I did hear that... that slapping sound.

227
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:30,720
But...

228
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,400
I honestly never saw who it was.

229
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,040
And anyway, that's one matter and this is another.

230
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,200
I figured...

231
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:41,600
if we talked it out in the open,

232
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,400
it wouldn't have to affect my son joining the factory.

233
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:55,040
So you're holding this over me, are you?

234
00:16:56,560 --> 00:16:57,840
Plain blackmail.

235
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,240
If I let your son into the factory,

236
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,840
you saw nothing.

237
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:03,160
If I don't let Wang Yang in,

238
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:06,200
you figure you can use it to smear me whenever you like.

239
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,240
That's the play, isn't it?

240
00:17:07,319 --> 00:17:08,960
No, Director.

241
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,280
I...

242
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:12,520
Master Wang, this conversation is over.

243
00:17:13,319 --> 00:17:15,160
-No, Director, you have to let me finish...
-Get out.

244
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:16,520
Get out.

245
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:27,599
Never mind "get out." You're going to let me finish.

246
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:29,920
Talk.

247
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,040
My father

248
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:38,080
was one of Hualin Steel's founding veterans.

249
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,960
I've been a model worker at the locomotive depot year after year.

250
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:45,960
And now, in my son's generation,

251
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:49,360
I won't stand for crooks framing him either.

252
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:53,800
If someone here is playing dirty tricks,

253
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:55,280
wrecking the factory and framing people,

254
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:57,960
then who ends up getting the hell out is anyone's guess.

255
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,040
Moral corruption! Sleeping around!

256
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,360
And you think you're in the right?

257
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,080
I'll report you!

258
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,600
To the union, the Women's Federation,

259
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,880
the newspapers, the radio, the TV station!

260
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:19,080
I'll damn well...

261
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:21,880
Brother-in-law, what are you fussing with?

262
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,360
N-nothing.

263
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:25,360
And you... what are you doing over here?

264
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:28,240
I... I'm just meeting a friend.

265
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:30,680
-Right, well...
-Right.

266
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,560
-All good?
-All... all good...

267
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,560
What's all that waving about?

268
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,680
I just hauled up two crates of beer.

269
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,160
My hands are a little sore, bro.

270
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:23,160
Just shaking them out.

271
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:24,960
I'll get back to work, bro.

272
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,120
Nobody leaves a drop tonight, got it?

273
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:45,640
-Of course.
-Come on... bottoms up.

274
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:49,880
-Fly, fly...
-Fly, fly...

275
